---
title: "Formula scoring"
description: "Shape QQL scores with arithmetic, payload fields, functions, decay, geo distance, and conditions."
sidebar:
  order: 6
---

Formula queries apply Qdrant score-builder expressions to prefetch scores or
payload fields.

{% qqlExample title="Prefetch then rescore" %}
WITH candidates AS (
  QUERY TEXT 'distributed systems' USING dense LIMIT 100
)
QUERY FORMULA
  $score * 0.8 + LOG(citation_count + 1) * 0.2
DEFAULTS (score = 0.0, citation_count = 0)
FROM papers
PREFETCH (candidates)
LIMIT 10;
{% /qqlExample %}

## Decay

{% qqlExample title="Freshness and popularity" %}
QUERY FORMULA
  $score
  + EXP_DECAY(age_days, TARGET = 0, SCALE = 30, MIDPOINT = 0.5)
  + GAUSS_DECAY(popularity, TARGET = 100, SCALE = 25)
DEFAULTS (score = 0.0, age_days = 365, popularity = 0)
FROM articles
LIMIT 10;
{% /qqlExample %}

Supported functions include `ABS`, `SQRT`, `LOG`, `LN`, `EXP`, `POW`,
`GEO_DISTANCE`, `EXP_DECAY`, `GAUSS_DECAY`, `LIN_DECAY`, `datetime`, and
`datetime_key`.

## Conditions

{% qqlExample title="Conditional score" %}
QUERY FORMULA
  CASE WHEN tier MATCH ANY ('premium')
    THEN $score * 1.5
    ELSE $score
  END
DEFAULTS (score = 0.0)
FROM docs
LIMIT 10;
{% /qqlExample %}
